{"id":"word:hebrew:H784","type":"word","title":"אֵשׁ","subtitle":"H784 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"fire (literally or figuratively)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֵשׁ (H784) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 378 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֵשׁ (ʼêsh) means fire (literally or figuratively) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 14 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֵשׁ","transliteration":"ʼêsh","pronunciation":"aysh","strong":"H784","lemmaId":"hebrew:H784","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["אֵ֖שׁ","בָּ/אֵֽשׁ","אֵשׁ֙","אֵ֣שׁ","בָּ/אֵ֔שׁ"],"morphs":[["HNcbsa",145],["HRd/Ncbsa",131],["HTd/Ncbsa",43],["HC/Ncbsa",16],["HR/Ncbsa",12],["HR/Ncbsc",11],["HNcbsc",9],["HC/Td/Ncbsa",3],["HNcbsc/Sp3ms",2],["HC/Rd/Ncbsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"fire (literally or figuratively)","usage":"burning, fiery, fire, flaming, hot.","full":"H784. esh אֵשׁ 377 noun feminine Exod 9:23 ( masculine Jer 48:45 ; Psa 104:4 ; ** masculine is dubious: Num 16:18 read עָלֶיהָ for 2nd עֲלֵיהֶם ( ᵐ5 B); Jer 20:9 see Ges § 132 d ; 48:45 read (many MSS., Num 21:23 ) יצאה ; Psa 104:4 read perhaps (Ol Du): לֵֹהטָה , or וָלָֽחַט ; Job 20:26 see Ges § 145 u (or 121 b) : compare Albr ZAW xvi {1896}. 63 . feminine & masculine Jer 20:9 ; Job 20:26 ) fire (Assyrian išatu COT Gloss , Syriac , Ethiopic derivatives from II. אנשׁ , , sociable, friendly element (MV Wetzst in De Psalmen, ed. 4, p. 888 Lag BN 68 compare , ), improbable especially in view of Assyrian; daghesh probably secondary; compare also Sta § 189 b ) — ׳א absolute Exod 9:24 +; construct Lev 6:2 + (seldom); suffix אִשּׁוֺ Deut 4:36 ; Job 18:5 ; אֶשְׁכֶם Isa 50:11 ; אִשָּׁם 66:24 ; &#8212; 1 fire , of conflagration, e.g. in briers, endangering or destroying crops קֹצִים וּמָֽצְאָה אֵשׁ תֵּצֵא Exod 22:5 ; compare 3:2 בָּאֵשׁ בֹּעֵר הַסְּנֶה (both E); more often of deliberate destruction by fire, especially בָּאֵשׁ שָׂרַף ( בָּ with qam. preton.) object golden calf 32:20 (J), other idols Deut 7:5 , 25 , Asherim 12:3 , chariots Josh 11:6 , 9 ; 2Kin 23:1 , house Judg 12:1 ; 14:15 , tower 9:52 , city-gates Neh 1:3 ; 2:3 , 13 , 17 , city Josh 6:24 ; Judg 18:27 compare Isa 1:7 +; also בְּ אֵשׁ שִׁלַּח Amos 1:4 , 7 , 10 +; בָּאֵשׁ אֶתהָֿעִיר שִׁלַּח Judg 1:8 ; 20:48 compare 2Kin 8:12 ; בָּאֵשׁ אֶתהָֿעִיר הִצִּית Josh 8:8 , 19 ; Jer 17:27 +, compare Judg 9:49 ; 2Sam 14:30-31 , (of field, compare Exod 22:5 above) 2 of supernatural fire, attending theophany Exod 3:2 ; 19:18 (both J E) Deut 4:11-12 , 15 , 33 , 36 +; specifically (הָ)אֵשׁ עַמּוּד Exod 13:21-22 , 14:24 (all J E) Neh 9:12 , 19 compare Deut 1:33 (see מַרְאֵהאֵֿשׁ Num 9:15-16 , P); of destructive fire from ׳י 11:1-2 , 3 (J) 26:10 (P) Lev 10:2 (P); compare ׳א אֹכֶלָת in simile of Yahweh's glory Exod 24:17 (E) Deut 4:24 ; 9:3 ; see also 1Kin 18:24 , 38 ; 2Kin 1:10 (twice in verse); 1:12 (twice in verse); 1:14 ; Job 1:16 (perhaps lightning intended), compare further of lightning Exod 9:23-24 , (JE) Psa 18:13 ; 18:14 ; 148:8 etc. 3 fire for cooking, roasting, parching , etc. אֵשׁ צְלִי roasted at a fire Exod 12:8-9 , (P) compare Lev 2:14 ; 2Chr 35:13 ; Isa 44:16 , 19 ; of tinder for lighting fire Gen 22:6-7 , (E); of fire for melting (gold for the idolatrous calf) Exod 32:24 ; for refining Jer 6:29 , where read with Qr עֹפֶרֶת תַּם מֵאֵשׁ ; compare Mal 3:2 (simile of purifying work of messenger of cov't). 4 especially of altar-fire Lev 1:7 (twice in verse); 6:2 ; 6:3 ; 6:5 ; 6:6 +; in offering incense 10:1 , also זָרָה אֵשׁ strange fire , i.e. an incense not commanded, offered presumptuously 10:1 ; Num 3:4 ; 26:61 ; fire from ׳י consuming sacrifice (compare 2 ) Lev 9:24 ; 2Chr 7:1 , 3 ; of fire in child-sacrifice (usually (לְׅ בָּאֵשׁ בֵּן הֶעֱבִיר ) 2Kin 16:3 ; 21:6 ; compare 17:17 ; 23:10 ; 2Chr 33:6 ; also בָּא ׳שׂרף 2Kin 17:31 , בָּא ׳בער 2Chr 28:3 . 5 figurative of Yahweh's anger Psa 89:47 (simile) compare Nahum 1:6 ; Lam 2:4 אֵשׁעֶֿבְרָתִי Ezekiel 21:36; Ezek 22:31 ; 38:19 , אֵשׁקִֿנְאָתִי 36:5 ; see also Isa 66:15 ; Psa 79:5 ; 89:47 etc.; of word of ׳י Jer 23:29 ; figurative of outbursting emotion Psa 39:4 ; of flagrant wickedness Isa 9:17 , etc: 6 in various combinations , אֵשׁ לַמִּיד Gen 15:17 (J) a torch of fire (compare Di); לַבַּתאֵֿשׁ Exod 3:2 flame of fire , אֵשׁ לַהַב Joel 2:5 , אֵשׁ לַמִּידֵי (in simile) Dan 10:6 compare Zech 12:6 , אֵשׁ לַהֲבוֺת Psa 29:7 אֵשׁ לַהֲבֵי Isa 66:15 compare ׳א לְהָבוֺת Psa 105:32 , א ׳נֹגַהּ לָהָבָה Isa 4:5 compare Hosea 7:6 ; אִשּׁוֺ שְׁבִיב spark of his fire Job 18:5 compare אֵשׁ כִּידוֺדֵי 41:11 ; אֵשׁ תַּנּוּר Psa 21:10 oven of fire , אֵשׁ כִּיּוֺר Zech 12:6 ; אֵשׁ אוֺר light of fire Psa 78:14 ; לֹהֵט אֵשׁ flaming fire 104:4 ; אֵשׁ לְשׁוֺן Isa 5:24 tongue of fire , אֵשׁ גַּחֲלֵי Ezek 1:13 coals of fire , so 10:2 , compare אֵשׁ רִשְׁמֵּי Song 8:6 ; on אֵשׁ אַבְנֵי Ezek 28:14 , 16 see אֶבֶן ; דַּת אֵשׁ Deut 33:2 , literally fire of a law , or fire was a law , but דָּת law is Persian & late; read perhaps דֹת [ לַמִּ ] אֵשׁ compare Exod 20:18 or דֶת [ יֹקֶ ] אֵשׁ compare Isa 65:5 . אֶשָּׁא noun [feminine] fire (Biblical Hebrew אֵשׁ ; K § 55, 5. 2 b thinks emphatic from onomatopoetic √ אשׁשׁ ; D 161 Buhl √ אשׁא compare אִישָּׁהָא אישָּׁא, ᵑ7 , Syriac ; — Dan 7:11 . אֻשַּׁיָּא אֻשֹּׁהִי, see [ אשׁ ]. above","rootNote":"a primitive word;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 14 12","keyReferences":["1Chr 14 12","1Chr 21 26","1Kgs 9 16","1Kgs 16 18","1Kgs 18 23","1Kgs 18 23","1Kgs 18 24","1Kgs 18 25"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":378,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 14 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":14,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/אֵֽשׁ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncbsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָ/אֵשׁ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncbsa"},{"referen